"""Layer 0, MLP down-projection, component 399: a "claim-framing word" detector.

It switches on for words that frame what is being said rather than what it is about:
  * hedges and reported evidence ("seems", "apparently", "maybe", "perhaps", "might",
    and 似乎 / 好像 / 或许 / 可能 ...), strength about 0.9;
  * "it turns out" and surprise words ("actually", "suddenly", "finally", 其实, 竟然,
    到底, 终于, 突然 ...), strength about 1.35, the strongest group;
  * "why / how / whether" question words ("why", 为什么, 怎么, 是否, 如何), about 1.2;
  * time-of-state adverbs ("recently", 最近, 一直, 通常, 目前 ...), about 0.95;
  * hesitation and the end of a reasoning block ("Hmm", "</think>"), about 0.86;
  * a weak group of other adverbs and degree words ("really", "sometimes", never, 也, 很,
